        "original_id": "7f91b15a-1c1c-5a2d-86c2-c8880b4aecd0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mike Connors, Leon Danielian\n- Roles: actor, private detective character, ballet dancer, teacher, choreographer, educator\n- Organizations: CBS\n- Products: Mannix\n- Awards: Golden Globe Award, Emmy Awards\n\nFacts:\n- Leon Danielian was an American ballet dancer, teacher, choreographer, and educator.\n- Mike Connors was born Krekor Ohanian on August 15, 1925, and he died on January 26, 2017.\n- Mike Connors was an Armenian-American actor best known for playing private detective Joe Mannix in the CBS television series Mannix from 1967 to 1975.\n- Mike Connors won a Golden Globe Award in 1970 for Mannix, the first of six straight nominations.\n- Mike Connors received four consecutive Emmy nominations from 1970 through 1973 for Mannix.\n- Leon Danielian was born on October 31, 1920, and he died on March 8, 1997.",
